# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AI tooling instructions and the lab notebook.
# AGENTS.md tells a coding agent how to work here; docs/ holds the environment
# archive, the decision log and the performance methodology. Both are working
# notes for whoever is building the lab — they change constantly and are not
# part of the published repository, so they stay local.
#
# Consequence: the published tree has to stand on its own. Environment traps
# belong in the comments of the code they affect, and anything a user of the
# repository needs belongs in README.md.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
GEMINI.md
.cursorrules
.cursor/
.aider*
.aiderignore
.github/copilot-instructions.md
/docs/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build trees.
# Everything nyx produces must stay inside the repository: the file sandbox
# denies writes anywhere else, so no build output belongs in ~/Library or /tmp.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.build/
.cache/
compile_commands.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Compilation artefacts.
# Covered by .build/ for in-tree builds; listed explicitly so an out-of-tree or
# editor-driven build cannot leak objects into the history either.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/
CMakeUserPresets.json
*.o
*.a
*.air
*.metallib
*.dSYM/
DerivedData/
xcuserdata/
*.xcuserstate

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Active-experiment switch (written by scripts/use.sh) and the convenience
# symlink that points at core/<active>. Both are local state, not source.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.nx-active
/entry

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Reproducible artefacts.
# Anything that can be regenerated from scenes + spp + seed stays out of git.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
outputs/*
!outputs/.gitkeep
reports/quality/*
!reports/quality/.gitkeep
reports/bench/*
!reports/bench/.gitkeep
references/_smoke/
references/_large/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Third-party sources downloaded at configure time. The registry in
# third_party/README.md is the source of truth for what these are.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
third_party/_deps/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# macOS / editors
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
*.swp
*.gputrace
